I've been using the ultra for one month  now and it's a great device but I wish I  could return it and it's not because  it's past the return policy which yeah  it is but it's because of multiple  usability issues Vadim reviewed the  ultra after one week of use and gave it  a raving review and I shot a bunch of  sweet Bureau shots for that which I'll  also share and use in this video but my  experience has been a bit different  because my review is not for those who  honestly just want to buy the Apple  watch Ultra for one simple reason it's  freaking cool now I completely agree  with pretty much everything that Vadim  said this was the most excited I have  been for an Apple Watch in many years  and even though I would have preferred a  square watch more like the leagues the  design is fresh and modern it is sporty  it looks industrial I do love that flat  top display and the crown guard also  looks industrial and it really minimize  how much fall Siri activations I got  when I'm having my hands on the ground  pushing against something I don't really  like the color of the action button but  it is very very useful to have I also  really like how loud and clear the  speakers are they are really really nice  for calls both for me to hear whoever  I'm talking to as well as for them to  hear me with those microphones now in  our Hands-On with the series 8 the  series 8 microphones actually sounded  better go ahead and take a listen this  is the microphone quality of the Apple  Watch series 8 and this is the quality  of the Ultras three microphones in a  room that doesn't have too much noise  now that is because the ultra chooses  which one of the three microphones to  use and here in our office it's not very  loud so I don't know what they chose but  in loud environments the ultra does a  better job now I also absolutely love  the haptics that are in this watch even  after a month I'm still surprised when  it goes and vibrates and notifies me how  much I feel that I can't miss it and  other people still don't hear that  vibration the red mode that is exclusive  to the ultra is also sweet and I use it  at night not to just save battery which  it does but because it is less  distracting now as far as a battery life  it is insane but I'll get back to that  in just a bit the new 2000 hits of  brightness on the display is also great  now I never complained about my previous  watches but it is nice to have in the  bright Sun now with that I do not love  the Alpine Loop now it holds really  great once you have it on but it's a  pain to put on it also can hit the  actual display in the body if you're  taking it off and putting it on a  charger and it's not that comfortable  after a while especially if that gets  wet now I also bought the diving Loop  but I don't really like using it either  now of course the Summer's kind of gone  so we're not swimming and boating as  much but for regular use putting it on  and off is a pain and I think that the  white also pops way too much compared to  the color of the watch so it's kind of  just sitting there don't get me wrong  both designs are great and they hold on  very well so they're doing what they're  designed to do but the Trail Loop sold  out instantly and even now the black and  gray one is still sold out so I can't  get one of them I'm still waiting on it  now I've tried a few third-party watch  bands and those aren't too bad but  because of the ultra being so tall it  basically makes the watch bands go  straight down if they're rubber or  different material and then you have  this Gap in between compared to you know  regular Apple watches where this pataka  carbon just wraps around so nicely it's  so lightweight and comfortable so  overall I just wish maybe we had more  choices from Apple now some people  complained about the price tag of 800  but my stainless steel with Milanese  Loop was 850 which now dropped in price  a bit so those are people who went out  and bought watches like this because  they are a lot more durable they will  not have an issue with the price now I'm  pretty hard on my watches and my  stainless steel one looks great compared  to my aluminum which dings and scratch  is super easy and the ion X glass which  sounds durable also scratches super easy  compared to the sapphire screen of the  stainless steel the ultra also has that  but because of the raised lip design  it's even more durable just watch Tech  racks smashing it with the hammer on his  desk and his desk breaks before the  watch does and even the internal parts  break before the screen cracks in the  last month I have slammed this thing  against doors and other objects with not  a single scratch or ding so it's  incredibly durable and the battery life  is tremendous even without the low power  mode which they showed off which is  going to give you like 60 hours of use I  finish off each day a normal day with  about 70 battery life remaining this is  something that Apple watch users have  been dreaming of for a long time now the  series 7 and 8 would still have good  battery life remaining at the end of the  day enough to do sleeve tracking and  then charge it in the morning but of  course that is with a brand new watch my  stainless steel now dies each day before  I go to bed which sucks and it is only a  few years old so the ultra will still  have great battery life even four to  five years from now which is another  great selling point now when I go out on  Long hikes the ultra can track my whole  day whereas I've had other ones die  before I am done so what do I not like  about it and why do I wish that I could  return it well one thing is Comfort I'm  used to the large size now it took about  a week and it's funny that the regular  watches feel small on my wrist now  overall it is less comfortable because  it is not only larger but also a lot  thicker so depending on what you're  wearing you know some longer shirts and  jackets they have a tough time slipping  over this watch and it really pops out  but another thing is sleep tracking now  I tried it out because the battery life  is great where my older one wasn't that  good and I cannot get used to it rolling  around in bed which I do I constantly  feel this thing now if that sounds funny  to you and like not a big deal MKBHD  actually switches out his watch band  each night and then again each morning  on his series seven just to get more  comfort for sleep tracking because of  that I'm not using this for sleep  tracking even though it seems like the  perfect device with great battery life  and the older watches were just so much  sleeker not only for sleep tracking but  just how they look on your wrist and  each time I grab this series eight with  this pataka watch band and I put it on I  just think man I wish that I could be  wearing that all the time this thing  just feels amazing on the hand  lightweight sleek and with that comes  looks now when I'm wearing an outfit  like this or with a jacket it looks  great it fits that normal kind of sporty  styling a t-shirt whatever but with  nicer looking clothes it just looks off  now I care about looks and the stainless  steel watches looked great with pretty  much anything that you wear especially  you know the gold one or you know any of  the other colors depending on what you  like because of this the ultra is  actually the watch that I've taken off  the most because it just doesn't look  good with a lot of things that I wear  now I really wish that this watch looked  a little bit less sporty like the leaks  we had for it and the Apple gave it  multiple color choices now sure keep the  plain Titanium because it's unpainted  it's the most durable but if Apple gave  us some options that would be really  nice the same thing goes with the size  now it's not too big for me and I got  used to it but for many other people it  just is and some people have returned it  because of that and honestly if Apple  could just give us better battery life  in a normal Apple watch which has a  lower price point that would be amazing  even if they had to cut out some of the  features to put in better battery life  now I know they talked about adding a  low power mode later but so many things  get shut off just take a look at this  list including getting text until you  actually press and turn on the watch to  get it to connect so from that point it  really doesn't make sense and it kind of  defeats the purpose of an Apple Watch  just to get better battery life so even  though I am using the ultra less than I  did my previous watches and I wish I  could return it the features and the  battery life just make it worth having  and I know that if I kept the series 8  and I use that instead there'd be many  times where I'd regret not having the  ultra so what I figured out that I'm  gonna do is keep my older gold stainless  steel watch because at this point I  looked up the resale value and it is  terrible and when I want a smart watch  and the ultra just doesn't look right I  will pop this thing on and use it and  that is a luxury I have as a tech  reviewer I already have the swatches  paid off but a lot of people don't have  that luxury so let's just hope that next  year the ultra will have other colors  than just the titanium and a smaller  size and just better battery life in  general for the normal Apple watches so  there you guys go that is my reasoning I  love this thing but there's always times  where I don't love it so much go ahead  and click that Circle above if you guys  want to see more videos check out  vadim's review right over there that's  been Max and I'll see you in the next  one  foreign
 

